  V3 [the honest statement] the phantom's re-settling clock is the merge ordering that distinguishes the sourced field from collisionless DM: the registered falsifier is ANY merger showing the dark-mass offset persisting AS LONG AS / LONGER than the baryonic gas's own re-alignment (the CDM-like slow re-attachment, t_dark >= t_gas) -- that leaves no fast R/c baryon-tracking phantom.  The framework predicts t_ph = 1.90 Myr << t_gas = 481 Myr and agrees with a PERSISTENT dark offset only when it is collisionless dust (S6: the Bullet's 8-sigma offset is dust-carried, kinematically realizable, phantom bounded at f_ph <= 0.125).  WHAT IS AND ISN'T ESTABLISHED, stated exactly: (1) the Bullet alone does NOT demonstrate the phantom-first ORDERING -- its offset is dust, expected to persist, so it does not separate t_ph < t_gas from t_dark >= t_gas (S6 V3's shared-with-CDM offset); (2) the second clock (t_sound = sqrt(2) t_dyn) is a re-arrangement clock of the phantom once sourced -- it does NOT move the offset, which is the dust's; the phantom is zero-offset on BOTH its clocks (S6 C3); (3) the discriminating observation is a merger pair caught in the window between t_ph and t_gas (~2 Myr .. ~1e8 yr) where the gas is still disrupted but the phantom has re-attached -- the seconds-available prediction of the sourced field; (4) the thick-era dust-clock reading (G111 N-body, t_cross 82 Myr) and the sound-clock reading are the framework's two independent ways to discriminate, and both are falsifiable against the collisionless baseline.

